 "rule": "register 1.6, v6.7 (1): the registered secondary view 'comparator from a near-miss source (not the cited reference) / normalised name / name bridge / note reading' -- a NOTE READING (v6.11 wording; v6.7 N6 called it a near-miss name source): the cited source's own module -- ref. 16, Gandal 2022, the reference Pagani cites -- reached through Gandal's Results text, not its printed label: Pagani's 'synaptic vesicles and plasticity' is no label Gandal's figures print (R-d, the primary record); Gandal's text describes GeneM5 as 'GeneM5 is downregulated in ASD, contains many neuronal genes involved in synaptic vesicle function, cytoskeleton and synaptic plasticity, and significantly overlaps with the downregulated synaptic module CTX.M16, previously identified by Parikshak et al. 5 in frontal and temporal cortex (Fig. 3a,d and Supplementary Data 5 and 6 ).' -- every content word of the name (plural / singular normalised) occurs in that description; v6.8 (C): the module is the one a content-word search of Gandal's article finds (exactly one, asserted); Pagani used 'co-expression modules of known biological function (n = 10)' (quoted)",
